> Can't CCD avoid tunneling issues when enabled regardless of the static body's thickness?

I must admit I thought it would be easier to force tunneling to happen without CCD, but when messing around with your MRP a bit I'm struggling to do so, and once I get to the kinds of velocities where tunneling does occur then enabling CCD (which only kicks in above a certain velocity) does indeed resolve it. Perhaps I'm not considering some common pitfall though.

@jrouwe If we only consider its use in a static body, is there any major difference between something like this and a triangle-based shape like `JPH::MeshShape`, in terms of risks of tunneling?
